data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1. Key breaking changes affecting your code:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | Removed — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Example = new OpenApiString(...)` | `schema.Example = JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — nullability via `schema.Type` flags (`JsonSchemaType.Null`) |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is a `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Now a class with `Scheme` and `Scopes` properties |
| `new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "..." }` | `new OpenApiReference("...", ReferenceType.SecurityScheme)` |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;       // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString → JsonValue
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        // OpenApiReference now takes (id, type) constructor args
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2", ReferenceType.SecurityScheme)
    };

    // OpenApiSecurityRequirement is no longer a dictionary —
    // it has Scheme + Scopes properties
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
        {
            Scheme = oAuthScheme,
            Scopes = scopes   // IList<string>
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable bool removed in OpenAPI 3.1; use Type flags instead.
                // Remove Null from the type set to make it non-nullable.
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of fixes:
1. **`using`** — Replace `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` with `System.Text.Json.Nodes`
2. **Example values** — `new OpenApiString("1.0")` → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")`
3. **References** — Use the new positional constructor `new OpenApiReference("oauth2", ReferenceType.SecurityScheme)`
4. **Security requirements** — Set `.Scheme` and `.Scopes` properties instead of dictionary indexing
5. **Nullable** — Replace `property.Value.Nullable = false` with clearing the `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag from `property.Value.Type`
